{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>המו</b> — It is possible that all that he mentioned is by way of allegory concerning the enemies, in the manner of \"then the waters would have swept us away\" [Psalms 124:4], or its meaning is: though the sea roar and the mountains quake at the pride of HaShem — so too the nations; therefore המו, they also מטו." "<b>תמוג</b> — The meaning reverses their [the mountains'] nature, which is exceedingly dry [i.e., solid]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "The reference is to Psalms 46:3 (\"though the mountains quake\"/\"the sea roars\"), implicitly cited here."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:03.624958704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}